{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Quick-start"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftcrossui\/quick-start"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Creating a cross-platform SwiftCrossUI app with Swift Bundler.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Quick start","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SwiftCrossUI"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Getting Started","generated":true,"anchor":"Getting-Started","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-development-environment","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-virtual-development-environment","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Examples","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Hot-reloading"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This quick start guide uses ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/stackotter\/swift-bundler","type":"reference"},{"text":". Although not strictly required, it simplifies many aspects of cross-platform distribution and provides a platform-agnostic configuration format for specifying things such as app icons and custom URL schemes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re new to Swift, we recommend starting with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-development-environment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Installing-Swift-Bundler","text":"Installing Swift Bundler","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Follow ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/stackotter\/swift-bundler?tab=readme-ov-file#installation-","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"mint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the preferred installation method on macOS and Linux as of the last update to this quick start guide.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Installing-system-dependencies","text":"Installing system dependencies","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each backend has different requirements. In this guide we’ll use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/DefaultBackend"},{"text":" which uses ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/AppKitBackend"},{"text":" on macOS, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend"},{"text":" on Linux, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/WinUIBackend"},{"text":" on Windows, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/UIKitBackend"},{"text":" on iOS\/tvOS. Click through the backend relevant to your machine for detailed installation requirements. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/AppKitBackend"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/UIKitBackend"},{"text":" have no system dependencies.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Using-Swift-Bundlers-SwiftCrossUI-template","text":"Using Swift Bundler’s SwiftCrossUI template","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Bundler provides many built-in templates; we’ll use the "},{"code":"SwiftCrossUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" template. The "},{"code":"SwiftCrossUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" template uses "},{"code":"DefaultBackend","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to select the most appropriate backend at compile time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"sh","code":["swift bundler create HelloWorld --template SwiftCrossUI","cd HelloWorld"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Running-your-app","text":"Running your app","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Running your new app with Swift Bundler is as simple as it gets!"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"sh","code":["swift bundler run"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On macOS you can provide the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--device <device_name_or_id>"},{"type":"text","text":" option to run the app on a connected iOS or tvOS device, or the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--simulator <simulator_name_or_id>"},{"type":"text","text":" option to run the app in a simulator."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"sh","code":["# You can use any substring of the target device name. For example,","# \"iPhone\" matches any device connected with \"iPhone\" in its name.","swift bundler run --device \"iPhone\"","swift bundler run --simulator \"iPhone 15\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Making-a-change","text":"Making a change","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/HelloWorld\/HelloWorldApp.swift"},{"text":" in an editor of your choosing. Change ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Hello, World!\""},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Hello, Earth!\""},{"text":". Repeat the previous step to verify that your changes get reflected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"All-done","text":"All done","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You’re good to go! If you make something cool with SwiftCrossUI l